From: Jordan Williams Johnson <jordandwj@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:09:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] etnaviv/ml: nn_layer_flush experiment hook, refused by
 default: it hangs (LLM engine, test tree only)

ETNA_ML_NO_FLUSH_INDEPENDENT clears nn_layer_flush on an NN job when the
next hardware job reads nothing written since the last flush (the
weight-group jobs of one LLM step). On the A311D's GC8000 that HUNG the
NPU on every invoke: "MMU 0 fault (page not present) addr 0x00000000",
20 recovered hangs (alta-npu incidents/2026-11-22-1526-LLMT-S2-noflush).
The bit is not a plain cache flush; without it the NN unit fetches
something at address 0. Kept for the record and refused unless the
variable is set to "I-know-it-hangs". Unset = unchanged, bit for bit.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
